{"title":"Mock AIME 3 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_3_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Circles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> are centered on opposite sides of line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" />, and are both tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05d0bb1172cf128548aec51cabd885258e296e6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> passes through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, intersecting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> again at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersections of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05d0bb1172cf128548aec51cabd885258e296e6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05d0bb1172cf128548aec51cabd885258e296e6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> respectively. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3bb4eeb347e74e025fd175c22f1f7275af0555e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/7/f874b39870586f0504f50a667f2bafedddf47904.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> are extended past <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and intersect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f796bce4821d96fe230af6de93e1028998df1d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = 3, AP = 6, DP = 4,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"207\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/3/fb37fd3129f1c9b2e447ed4d2ad51b6c7ac78026.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ = 32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"70\" height=\"16\" />, then the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/8/e0830febe7535fbbdf19782a978c79c0c9e6cd70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PBC$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/2/0e29a76216d1250df9f2d45380bb908ccf2d1c86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{p\\sqrt{q}}{r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"35\" height=\"38\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/c/0ec2b6f850a38c18bff9b2d860b248982102966e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p, q,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"31\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are positive integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are coprime and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is not divisible by the square of any prime. Determine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/d/70d212c459fbffb5d5822c41ea9d670acfe19b26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p + q + r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_3_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AIME_2005_14a.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/1/18/AIME_2005_14a.png/600px-AIME_2005_14a.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"600\" height=\"441\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/1/18/AIME_2005_14a.png/900px-AIME_2005_14a.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/1/18/AIME_2005_14a.png/1200px-AIME_2005_14a.png 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/f/6ff78a5d17051e030508cf543f4772cfa665f413.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1, O_2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43b6f63aa2266ef1b39b31386bd17b28e25faaac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> be the centers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/8/178ef0c25cb393195368ae91e70341404562e677.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1, \\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05d0bb1172cf128548aec51cabd885258e296e6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> respectively.\n</p><p>Let point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/e/3be5b2b1c5702a00b8442d62d03534e3a0a0f4be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" />.  Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/0/260a49ed764434b98da3f3c48e2a5567f4bf7cfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_3R \\bot PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/4/f948659b4fa8d5066e0c719d6d26066d9d0a60c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|PR|=\\frac{|PQ|}{2}=16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"149\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/c/adc143c3f887fa7e92fd80d91bb22af51b4abd77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b4f3f4b698ce35667432041e168f7653533fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> be the radii of circles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> respectively.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c7f3f828cf12ab9cafeffad282468a95219600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/a/e3a8ae66ded7f33f9385a37c9cadfb82720013d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> be the areas of triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/9/249e729f8542ff5cfba842850a5efd1bc66e217e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PDA$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/8/e0830febe7535fbbdf19782a978c79c0c9e6cd70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PBC$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> respectively.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/8/f089ac08b0599a8fa3bcdcbab7008258cc8e4a30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_3R \\parallel O_1O_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"99\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/c/5bceb784d5537fd6db760e214b90da5de741e78a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle RO_3O_2 = \\angle O_3O_2O_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"172\" height=\"17\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/6/3162b35b21598ffe3d8da859ff08d5ba9842d7e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_2B \\parallel O_1D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"94\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/6/dc6252e4d8b8f348b6822d4b256a1a87e759e957.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC \\parallel AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/7/e87a8180c41d5a6c8e1dd34a6de2d1392aad2246.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta PDA \\sim \\Delta PBC \\sim \\Delta O_3O_1O_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"246\" height=\"17\" />.  In other words, those three triangles are similar.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/c/adc143c3f887fa7e92fd80d91bb22af51b4abd77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> is the circumcenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/9/b49c6591b5cca6db1337229d91522153ffc88884.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta PDA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />, \n</p><p>then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/d/28d81a1ccabd454c98e2ccdc0022fbebe6bbd3bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1=\\frac{|AD| \\times |DP| \\times |AP|}{4A_1}=\\frac{(3)(4)(6)}{4A_1}=\\frac{18}{A_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"354\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/d/32d78aae1741ff43c6f40e2077f1ab67900cca2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> be the height of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/9/b49c6591b5cca6db1337229d91522153ffc88884.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta PDA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> to side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/4/37440356a88846b89b9fdd6cee1e944e2aa4b6b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1=\\frac{|AD| \\times h_1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"131\" height=\"40\" />, thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/c/c2c44d85516bcebaec28f01192ea55c8fc0b3a33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_1=\\frac{2}{3}A_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"78\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/6/ec6916b50feec24773d374eaada26a95bcabc6fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PR$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> is the height of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/0/cc02a20305696b88e26eab2d88cdead513a971ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta O_1O_2O_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"17\" /> to side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/7/127e372b5c305f6505bc9497ec419dbe77565fbe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1O_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" />, then using similar triangles, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/f/48ff444ac320b9e46c5bdbab6d843e40e45bde89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{|O_1O_2|}{|PR|}=\\frac{|AD|}{h_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"126\" height=\"45\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/41291e721cb331e2cc3d6b9266b6daa43a780f8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{r_1+r_2}{16}=\\frac{3}{\\frac{2}{3}A_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"119\" height=\"45\" />.  Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b4f3f4b698ce35667432041e168f7653533fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b1306cf1102f6ad1bfb8ec66ea45fcbb3fda1e90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_2=\\frac{72}{A_1}-r_1=\\frac{72}{A_1}-\\frac{18}{A_1}=\\frac{54}{A_1}=3\\left( \\frac{18}{A_1} \\right)=3r_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"387\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>By similar triangles,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c78623e7a32ecb0bb356a5eb15b7ca6ddb9f8a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_2=\\left( \\frac{r_2}{r_1} \\right)^2A_1=9A_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"179\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>Using Heron's formula,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/a/87a5732756c9c002a6875161428f9db6695f94db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1=\\sqrt{s(s-a)(s-b)(s-c)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"233\" height=\"35\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/d/31d8df3813ff8140ab0dc143f0ab7ce29647907e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s=\\frac{a+b+c}{2}=\\frac{3+6+4}{2}=\\frac{13}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"255\" height=\"39\" /> we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/e/03e52c58f7e89da93cc9049e316bc3719a5bf674.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1=\\sqrt{\\left( \\frac{13}{2} \\right)\\left( \\frac{13}{2}-3\\right)\\left( \\frac{13}{2}-6 \\right)\\left( \\frac{13}{2}-4 \\right)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"361\" height=\"56\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/2/df261998fb9a3c61acdaa91bad5a05cc9c300a98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1=\\frac{\\sqrt{\\left(13\\right)\\left(7\\right)\\left(1\\right)\\left(5\\right)}}{4}=\\frac{\\sqrt{455}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"251\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/2/1e2571a97a62f6bdabcfa9b2ec41c655a6fd4d6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_2=9A_1=\\frac{9\\sqrt{455}}{4}=\\frac{p\\sqrt{q}}{r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"218\" height=\"43\" />, thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/f/befdf739f1fa1940e4a86f068a5fa90dd09239dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=9,q=455,r=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"163\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/0/5805335a6405e44a3acc8f507871c2155409cb06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+q+r=\\boxed{468}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"136\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~Tomas Diaz. orders@tomasdiaz.com\n</p><p><i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_3_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_3_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_3_Pre_2005\" title=\"Mock AIME 3 Pre 2005\">Mock AIME 3 Pre 2005</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_3_Pre_2005_Problems\" title=\"Mock AIME 3 Pre 2005 Problems\">Problems</a></b>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?t={{{source}}}\">Source</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_3_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"Mock AIME 3 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_3_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"Mock AIME 3 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_3_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"Mock AIME 3 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_3_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"Mock AIME 3 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_3_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"Mock AIME 3 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_3_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"Mock AIME 3 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_3_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"Mock AIME 3 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b